om/wp/media/white-album-portrait-paul-mccartney-404x580.jpg 404w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/white-album-portrait-paul-mccartney-669x960.jpg 669w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/white-album-portrait-paul-mccartney-768x1103.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/white-album-portrait-paul-mccartney-1070x1536.jpg 1070w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/white-album-portrait-paul-mccartney.jpg 1172w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 139px) 100vw, 139px\" data-attachment-id=\"23422\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1968-photos/white-album-portrait-paul-mccartney/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/white-album-portrait-paul-mccartney.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1172,1683\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-comments-count=\"1\" data-image-title=\"White Album portrait: Paul McCartney\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/white-album-portrait-paul-mccartney-669x960.jpg\" /></a></div></figure><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon portrait'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1968-photos/white-album-portrait-george-harrison/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIxMzkiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMTM5IDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"139\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/white-album-portrait-george-harrison-139x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"White Album portrait: George Harrison\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/white-album-portrait-george-harrison-139x200.jpg 139w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/white-album-portrait-george-harrison-404x580.jpg 404w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/white-album-portrait-george-harrison-669x960.jpg 669w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/white-album-portrait-george-harrison-768x1103.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/white-album-portrait-george-harrison-1070x1536.jpg 1070w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/white-album-portrait-george-harrison.jpg 1182w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 139px) 100vw, 139px\" data-attachment-id=\"23420\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1968-photos/white-album-portrait-george-harrison/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/white-album-portrait-george-harrison.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1182,1697\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"White Album portrait: George Harrison\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/white-album-portrait-george-harrison-669x960.jpg\" /></a></div></figure><figure class='gallery-item'><div class='gallery-icon portrait'>\n<a href='https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1968-photos/white-album-portrait-ringo-starr/'><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIxMzkiIGhlaWdodD0iMjAwIiB2aWV3Qm94PSIwIDAgMTM5IDIwMCI+PHJlY3Qgd2lkdGg9IjEwMCUiIGhlaWdodD0iMTAwJSIgZmlsbD0iI2NmZDRkYiIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"139\" height=\"200\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/white-album-portrait-ringo-starr-139x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"White Album portrait: Ringo Starr\" data-srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/white-album-portrait-ringo-starr-139x200.jpg 139w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/white-album-portrait-ringo-starr-404x580.jpg 404w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/white-album-portrait-ringo-starr-669x960.jpg 669w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/white-album-portrait-ringo-starr-768x1103.jpg 768w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/white-album-portrait-ringo-starr-1070x1536.jpg 1070w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/white-album-portrait-ringo-starr.jpg 1175w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 139px) 100vw, 139px\" data-attachment-id=\"23423\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/gallery/1968-photos/white-album-portrait-ringo-starr/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/white-album-portrait-ringo-starr.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"1175,1687\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"White Album portrait: Ringo Starr\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/white-album-portrait-ringo-starr-669x960.jpg\" /></a></div></figure></div><p>The album&#8217;s simple title \u2013 <em>The Beatles</em> \u2013 was also suggested by Hamilton.</p><blockquote><div>Richard asked, &#8216;Has there been an album called <em>The Beatles</em>?&#8217; so I referred back to EMI and they said, &#8216;No. There&#8217;s been <a href=\"/albums/meet-the-beatles/\"><em>Meet The Beatles!</em></a>, <a href=\"/albums/introducing-the-beatles/\"><em>Introducing The Beatles</em></a> in America, but there&#8217;d never been an album called <em>The Beatles</em>.&#8217; So he said, &#8216;Let&#8217;s call it that&#8217;; which is the official title of the <em>White Album</em>.</div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">Paul McCartney<br />\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/manyyearsfromnow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Many Years From Now</em></a></div><p>The white cover concept went through several revisions, one of which was to have the green stain of an apple.</p><blockquote><div>Richard had a friend from Iceland, the artist Dieter Roth, who used to send him letters smeared in chocolate, and Richard liked that a lot, so then the idea grew; he said, &#8216;Well, maybe we could do something like that with an apple. We could bounce an apple on a bit of paper and get a smudge, a very light green smear with a little bit of pulp.&#8217; But we ended up thinking that might be hard to print, because inevitably if these things do well, there are huge printings in places like Brazil and India and anything too subtle like a little apple smear can be lost, can just look like they printed it crappy. So that idea went by the wayside.</p><p>So now he was saying, &#8216;Let&#8217;s call it <em>The Beatles</em> and have it white, really white.&#8217; I was saying, &#8216;Well, I dunno. It&#8217;s a great concept, but we are releasing an album here. This is not a piece of art for a rather elite gallery, this is more than that. I see the point. It&#8217;s a nice idea, but for what we were to people, and still are, it doesn&#8217;t quite fit, we&#8217;re not quite a blank space, a white wall, the Beatles. Somebody ought to piss on it or smudge an apple on it for it to become the Beatles, because a white wall&#8217;s just too German and marvellous for us.&#8217; So the idea then emerged to do the embossing. &#8216;Maybe if we emboss the word &#8220;Beatles&#8221; out of the white, that&#8217;ll be good. We&#8217;ll get a shadow from the embossing but it&#8217;s white on white. It&#8217;s still white. That&#8217;ll be nice.&#8217; But I still wanted something on the white, an idea, like the apple smudging.</div></blockquote><div class=\"source\">Paul McCartney<br />\n<a href=\"https://geni.us/manyyearsfromnow\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><em>Many Years From Now</em></a></div><div class=\"page-links\">Pages: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/albums/the-beatles-white-album/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">1</span></a> <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/albums/the-beatles-white-album/2/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">2</span></a> <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/albums/the-beatles-white-album/3/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">3</span></a> <span class=\"post-page-numbers current\" aria-current=\"page\"><span class=\"page-link\">4</span></span> <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/albums/the-beatles-white-album/5/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">5</span></a> <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/albums/the-beatles-white-album/6/\" class=\"post-page-numbers\"><span class=\"page-link\">6</span></a></div>",
